knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3759 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3756)
What it fixes: a tsconfig `paths` entry with several targets (`"@lib/*": ["lib/a/*", "lib/b/*"]`) only
used its first target, so an import that exists only under a later target failed to build
(`Could not load .../lib/a/b-only`), and a `.d.ts` target was used as a module. Next.js tries each
target in order and skips `.d.ts` targets (Next.js e2e `typescript-paths`). The alias resolver now
tries the remaining targets when the first does not resolve, and `.d.ts` targets are dropped.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3759.
Ported by hand from the upstream src change to the published 1.0.1 dist files.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

